tDD - 2t values over all iso classes n=3..5: [0, 1]
claim trans(D(D(T))) >= 2*trans(T): violations = 0

--- tower cores ---
T3: t=2  trans(D(D(T3)))=5  2t+1=5  [tower T15: trans=5 on 15 vertices]
T7: t=3  trans(D(D(T7)))=7  2t+1=7  [tower T31: trans=7 on 31 vertices]
T15: t=5  trans(D(D(T15)))=11  2t+1=11  [tower T63: trans=11 on 63 vertices]

CONCLUSION: D(D(.)) always doubles trans (within +1) at n<=5; equals 2t+1 on
tower cores; T_{4m+3} = D(D(T_m)) + 3 pivots and the pivots add nothing,
giving the exact two-step recursion trans(level k) = 2*trans(level k-2) + 1.

